<title>JAPAN: Nakamichi bid-only on stock allocation.</title>
<headline>Nakamichi bid-only on stock allocation.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in a Japanese audio equipment maker Nakamichi Corp were bid-only on Monday morning, supported by news that the firm would allocate 64 million new shares to a Singapore unit of Hong Kong's Grande Holdings Ltd in January, brokers said.</p>
<p>The share price was bid-only at 655 yen at 0122 GMT, against Friday's 615 yen.</p>
<p>The Japanese business daily Nihon Keizai Shimbun said over the weekend that Nakamichi would become a member of the Grande group as a result of the issue because the latter would own a 70.3 percent stake in Nakamichi.</p>
</text>
